# ── NOT PART OF THE PUBLIC SITE ──────────────────────────────────────────
# The repo root is the deploy root, so every project document beside the HTML
# is served too unless it is blocked here. These are internal: README carries
# the launch-blocker list, OFFERS and BRIEF carry unshipped positioning, and
# _parked/ holds the case-study fold that was lifted out precisely BECAUSE it
# names clients without written permission. Publishing it at a guessable URL
# would undo the reason for parking it.
#
# 404 rather than 301: these should read as not existing, not as moved.
# Above every other rule, because first match wins.
/README.md          /404.html   404
/OFFERS.md          /404.html   404
/BRIEF.md           /404.html   404
/COPY.md            /404.html   404
/CLAUDE.md          /404.html   404
/JOURNAL.md         /404.html   404
/PHOTOGRAPHY.md     /404.html   404
/A2P-COMPLIANCE.md  /404.html   404
/build.py           /404.html   404
/layout-check.js    /404.html   404
/_parked/*          /404.html   404
/serve.py           /404.html   404
# lib/ is NOT blocked as a directory — circuit.css and circuit.js are loaded
# by the pages. Only its own README is internal.
/lib/README.md      /404.html   404
# The case-study screenshots belong to the fold parked in _parked/. They are
# named client sites, referenced by nothing, and reachable at a guessable URL
# — blocking the markup and publishing the pictures would leave the same hole.
/assets/studies/*   /404.html   404

# Redirects from the old WordPress site to this one.
#
# Cloudflare Pages reads this file. Format is: <from> <to> <status>, first match
# wins, so specific rules must sit above the wildcards.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The site this replaces has been indexed for years and
# was still live on 2026-08-28 — WordPress 7.1, Elementor, AIOSEO, titled
# "Reptify Media - Best Digital Marketing Company New York". Search Console shows
# 3,353 impressions in the four weeks to 27 August across 66 queries. All of that
# accrues to the OLD urls. Deploying this site without a map would 404 every one
# of them, and a 404 tells Google the page is gone rather than moved: the ranking
# is not transferred, it is discarded. A 301 passes it on.
#
# The old canonical form carries NO trailing slash — /about-us returns 200,
# /about-us/ 301s to it, and the canonical tags agree. Both forms are listed
# anyway, because inbound links from other people's sites will use whichever
# they happened to copy, and we do not control those.
#
# All of these were verified live (HTTP 200) on 2026-08-28 before being mapped.

# ── pages with a direct equivalent ─────────────────────────
/about-us                 /about.html      301
/about-us/                /about.html      301
/contact-us               /contact.html    301
/contact-us/              /contact.html    301
/blog                     /journal.html    301
/blog/                    /journal.html    301
/terms-of-service         /terms.html      301
/terms-of-service/        /terms.html      301
/privacy-policy           /privacy.html    301
/privacy-policy/          /privacy.html    301

# The old /services page has no single equivalent: this site splits that job
# across four offer pages plus the Solution fold on the homepage. Sending it to
# the fold keeps the reader in the same conceptual place rather than picking one
# offer arbitrarily. If /services turns out to carry real ranking — check
# Search Console before deciding — a proper services index is worth building,
# and this line should then point at it.
/services                 /#solutions      301
/services/                /#solutions      301

# Affiliate terms: no equivalent page exists yet and the affiliate programme is
# an open decision. Terms is the nearest honest destination. Revisit if the
# programme ships.
/affiliate-terms-and-conditions   /terms.html   301
/affiliate-terms-and-conditions/  /terms.html   301

